  "name": "cube-3d",
  "$comment": "Plan 9.9 (X5.4): a 0.15 m cube balanced on one corner by three body-axis reaction wheels, equation-block plant (library/CornerCube.jl) and a 2 ms discrete LQR (library/CubeLQR.jl, K from design/design.py). The motors are the stdlib drives/ElectricDrive with the stator fixed (the reaction torque is inside the block); the motor rotor inertia J_m = 1e-6 kg m^2 (rotating relative to the cube) is the smallest value that keeps the solver robust, J_m <= 1e-8 makes the re-initialisation at the controller ticks fail (derivative causality of the rotor against the rate-imposed wheel). The position of the 3D pose binding comes from the three constant blocks PosX/Y/Z (inline, output unit m, which the pose binding requires) (the pivot corner is the world origin).",
