        "id": "a1",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Corner-balancing cube (plan 9.9). Cube (project block CornerCube): rigid body on a ball joint at the corner (world origin), 3 reaction wheels on the body axes; hand-derived dynamics with quaternion, body rates and relative wheel rates as states. Each wheel is driven by an ElectricDrive (R 1 ohm, L 0.1 mH, k 0.0335) whose stator is fixed: the reaction torque on the cube is already inside the block. Ctrl (CubeLQR): 2 ms discrete LQR on [tilt(2), rates(3), wheel rates(3)], gains from design/design.py, voltage limit +-12 V. Start: 2 degrees off the vertical about the world x axis.",
